Cell["\<\
\"\[Delta]\" gives the contribution on the worldline. Note that we keep the \
DiracDelta whereas we don't keep the HeavisideTheta in \
\"ExtendedHomogeneous\". This is because for other sources there might be \
DiracDelta' terms and we want to keep that option open for the future. \
\>", "ExampleText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.942310233174951*^9, 3.9423104174852247`*^9}, {
   3.947075556004992*^9, 3.947075579156873*^9}, 3.947426452602668*^9, {
